      "writtenOn": "2025-05-13T14:35:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Tim for reference .\n\n\"Today\u0027s linux-next merge of the drm-intel tree got a conflict in:\n\n  drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_mst.c\n\nbetween commit:\n\n  6fe7b1d10cbd (\"drm/i915/dp_mst: Expose a connector to kernel users after it\u0027s properly initialized\")\n\nfrom the drm-misc tree and commits:\n\n  529798bd786a (\"drm/i915/mst: convert to struct intel_display\")\n  d58f65df2dcb (\"drm/i915/dp_mst: Fix connector initialization in intel_dp_add_mst_connector()\")\n  fdb65ede8a45 (\"drm/i915/mst: unify MST connector function naming to mst_connector_*\")\"\n  \nAs the original issue happened when \"dp_mst: Expose a connector to kernel users after it\u0027s properly initialized \" is not merging cleanly when drm-intel and drm-misc merging to linux-next  , done similar changes in patch \"dp_mst: Expose a connector to kernel users after it\u0027s properly initialized\" and i am abandoning this patch .\n\nNow i am hitting below error when pushing the new patchset( because of reorder my patches not applying on george\u0027s tree . Please help to change the gerrit setting (refer below link) so i can push rebased set\n\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/43226755/push-patchset-to-gerrit-own-by-another-author",
